{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Repeated Problem Detector",
  "description": "When the user says a previous fix failed or the same problem persists, forces the agent to change diagnostic strategy instead of repeating superficial fixes.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "promptSubmit"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "RECURRENCE CHECK. Inspect the user's most recent message. Trigger this only if the user explicitly indicates that a previous attempted fix failed or that the same problem persists. Examples: 'sigue fallando', 'otra vez', 'mismo error', 'ya lo intentamos', 'no funcionó', 'sigue igual', 'same error', 'still failing', 'again', 'regression'. If triggered, do not propose another fix immediately. First produce four sections: 1) PREVIOUS ATTEMPT: what was previously tried or assumed. 2) CURRENT EVIDENCE: reproduce or verify the current failure using the best available project-specific method; do not invent commands. 3) FALSE ASSUMPTION: explain what the failed attempt proves false. 4) NEW HYPOTHESIS: propose a different causal hypothesis and the smallest validation needed. Only after those four sections may you modify code. If no recurrence is present, ignore this hook."
  }
}